Thanks for your responses. To be honest, I do not have a strong programming background or deep knowledge of Bayesian statistics, so a lot of what's in the manual went over my head. For example, I'm not yet clear on what is meant by "...increment the total model log probability with log foo(x|theta)." and why this means that "x must already be set." But, I will look back at the manual and continue working on my understanding.

One thing I want to be clear on: if I do marginilize 'Z' out of the log probability function, will this model work or do I need an alternative that does not involve explicitly defining 'Z'? You mentioned that local integer parameter values are initialized at 0, which would definitely not work with this model, because when a species is observed at a site, Z must equal 1 at that site. So, the question is, will marginilization of Z as described in the manual take care of this problem, or is this model simply a no-go in the current version of STAN?

Thanks again for all your help.

