n 1/6/14, 7:08 PM, Shravan Vasishth wrote:
> Is there an example available, e.g., with the schools data?
>
> On Monday, January 6, 2014 5:37:35 AM UTC+1, Shravan Vasishth wrote:
>
>     In the BDA 3rd edition book there are examples of posterior predictive model checks for the school data, also in
>     Appendix C. But these are done in R, not within Stan. I want to be able to generate the distribution of the maximum
>     values from predicted data within Stan. I saw in a post from 2012 that this was not possible to do (or maybe I
>     misunderstood this).   Is it possible to do now? Is there an example available that generates future data?

I'll add a simple example in the next edition of the manual.

We added a generated quantities block that makes it easier
to do posterior predictive checks efficiently that independently
sample the posterior predictive quantities from each sample.
They're effectively "cut" from the model.

We discuss this in the manual, but the only example is a
complex one for Gaussian processes in section 16.4.

(Without more context, I won't be able tof ind the old post you're
referring to.)

- Bob

