From ua387d7985c232d82 at groups.google.com  Fri Jan 17 18:25:22 2014
From: ua387d7985c232d82 at groups.google.com (Devin Caughey)
Date: Fri, 17 Jan 2014 18:25:22 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-users] DLM for Proportions/Multinomial Model
Message-ID: <IpFRiQFFYps.ynAz0OGtFUUJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <IpFRiQFFYps.iUqOAfDdoTUJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <IpFRiQFFYps.c71r2wuq7xAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <IpFRiQFFYps.iUqOAfDdoTUJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/IpFRiQFFYps/m/ynAz0OGtFUUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Bob,

Thanks for the correction. Your math is correct. The updated code is:

    int<lower=1> T; // number of time periods
    int<lower=1> K; // number of categories
    int<lower=0> counts[T, K];
}
parameters {
    simplex[K] props[T]; // period-specific category proportions
    real<lower=0> tau; // innovation standard deviation
}
transformed parameters {
    vector[K] logit_props[T]; // logit of proportions
    for (t in 1:T) {
        for (k in 1:K) {
            logit_props[t, k] <- logit(props[t, k]);
            // Adjust for logit tranform by incrementing the log probability

            // by the log of the derivative of the logit function
            increment_log_prob(-(log(props[t, k]) + log1m(props[t, k])));

        }
    }
}
model {
    for (t in 1:T) {
        if (t > 1) {
            logit_props[t] ~ normal(logit_props[t - 1], tau);
        }

        counts[t] ~ multinomial(props[t]);
    }
}

Devin

