I interpreted you to mean defining your own functions in C++
and then interfacing them with Stan.  I'd start here if that's
your goal:  https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/wiki/Contributing-New-Functions-to-Stan

If you mean do we have plans to add a way to define functions within
the Stan language, yes, that's hopefully something we'll roll out this
year.  The problem's going to be that it won't be much use if the
functions can't be independently tested / debugged.

- Bob

