Because the simplex is compact, you get a proper uniform prior
on it.  Same as for correlation matrices and unit-length vectors.

I'm pretty sure there's a proper prior on the unconstrained space
through the Jacobian.  If not, we've (or at least I've) been
giving people bad advice on the list.

Practically speaking, there's no issue at all just sampling
from a simplex with no priors declared in Stan.  It mixes
very well.

- Bob

