they're trying to do.

You're right that we don't have the inverse cumulative distribution
functions (CDFs).  We also don't have any way to first fit just marginals
and use those marginal fits to fit correlations, but I'll take a look
at the Michael Smith paper on Bayesian approaches to copulas (the
arXiv link).

As an aside, we're using the Joe et al. vine approach in our transforms
for modeling correlation matrices;  see the chapter of the manual on
transforms and Jacobians near the end of the manual.

- Bob

