>
> with the interpretation
>
>    p(theta|..., ...) = foo(theta|...) * bar(theta|...)
>
> you can just write it as above.

Poole and Raftery  recommend logarithmic pooling of priors, and advocate
a mixing proportion of 0.5. ie.

p(theta|..., ...) = foo(theta|...)^0.5  *  bar(theta|...)^(1-0.5)

